{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And he called the name of the place HaShem Yir'eh, which is said today, on the mountain of HaShem Yera'eh.</b> Since it is stated (Exodus 34:23) ״יֵרָאֶה כָּל זְכוּרְךָ״, read it as both ״יִרְאֶה״ (He will see) and ״יֵרָאֶה״ (He will be seen) — the yod in tsere — to say that just as He comes to be seen, so He comes to see. Thus it is stated here as well, in this same vein, ״יִרְאֶה״ and ״יֵרָאֶה״, for it is all one matter. But in order to settle the phrase ״אֲשֶׁר יֵאָמֵר הַיּוֹם״, I say that he called the name of the place ״ה׳ יִרְאֶה״ — which connotes the future — because this holy place the Holy One, blessed be He, did not reveal to any creature: for even to Abraham it was said, ״עַל אַחַד הֶהָרִים אֲשֶׁר אֹמַר אֵלֶיךָ״ (Genesis 22:2), and we do not find that He said anything to him beyond what Abraham perceived through seeing a cloud bound upon the mountain; but in any case there is no explicit statement and no words that this is the mountain which Elohim desired for His dwelling. For HaShem concealed it for the reason that will be explained (Deuteronomy 12:4) with the help of HaShem. Therefore he called it ״ה׳ יִרְאֶה״, in the language of ״אֱלֹהִים יִרְאֶה לּוֹ הַשֶּׂה״ (Genesis 22:8) — thus he said that a time would come when HaShem would see and choose this place, and at that time it would be said to the generations, ״הַיּוֹם בְּהַר ה׳ יֵרָאֶה״ — today, and not before, for until the day it was chosen, the Holy One, blessed be He, had not revealed it."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The acronym בעזה״י (בעזרת השם יתברך, 'with the help of HaShem, blessed be He') is expanded in translation to 'with the help of HaShem.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:29:13.037463510Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}